DIRECTOR_BRIEF={{ JSON.stringify($('Director Sprint Input').item.json.body ?? $('Director Sprint Input').item.json) }}
RECOVERY_CONTEXT={{ JSON.stringify($json.recovery_context ?? null) }}
When recovery context is present, preserve the same Director objective and constraints while reducing complexity. It is advisory and cannot override scope or safety. Include it verbatim in recovery_context_acknowledged.
PAST LESSONS — do not repeat these mistakes (advisory only, max 5): []
Return JSON only:
{"objective":"...","scope":["..."],"requirements":["..."],"assumptions":["..."],"ambiguities":["..."],"acceptance_criteria":["..."],"constraints":["..."],"known_context":["..."],"recovery_context_acknowledged":null,"status":"READY|BLOCKED","blocker":"NONE or concise reason"}
If the objective is absent, return BLOCKED. Never claim facts not present in the brief.

